[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2867737480","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106181#issuecomment-2867737480","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106181","id":2867737480,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6q7jOI","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-09T19:47:13Z","updated_at":"2025-05-09T19:48:48Z","body":"The `Change` text is correct, the actual problem is that EditorInterface popups the dialog with `p_replace_mode` being true, which does not make sense.\r\n\r\nEDIT:\r\nActually it makes sense _partially_. The `popup_create_dialog()` has `p_current_type` parameter. The dialog should open in change mode only if that argument is non-empty.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2867737480/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868679625","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106181#issuecomment-2868679625","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106181","id":2868679625,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6q_JPJ","user":{"login":"SirLich","id":18729296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NzI5Mjk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18729296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich","html_url":"https://github.com/SirLich","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SirLich/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-10T09:32:55Z","updated_at":"2025-05-10T09:32:55Z","body":"@KoBeWi I am using `current_type` to select the default selected node in my [addon](https://github.com/SirLich/godot-create-actor). This is because I desire to set `Node2D` as the default (`Node` as base). I might also cache the users selection so that future dialogues will use their last selected type.\r\n\r\nIn my opinion, the text `Change` isn't particularly compelling, even in the \"happy path\" where you are using this dialogue to change a nodes type. \r\n\r\nFor example:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aadfc29a-1c71-47be-81b4-76602491705a)\r\n\r\nThis isn't [Delete] [Cancel] it's [OK] [Cancel]\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2868679625/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2873663805","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106181#issuecomment-2873663805","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106181","id":2873663805,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rSKE9","user":{"login":"manchere","id":11008910,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDA4OTEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11008910?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/manchere","html_url":"https://github.com/manchere","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manchere/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manchere/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manchere/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manchere/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manchere/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manchere/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manchere/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manchere/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manchere/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-12T18:51:09Z","updated_at":"2025-05-12T18:51:09Z","body":"One solution is to introduce `p_replace_mode` parameter to `popup_create_dialog` so that users can set it to true or false to explicitly choose between `Change` or `Create`. \r\n\r\nThis way users can specify a `p_current_type` value in create mode as well without hitting `Change` all the time. \r\n\r\nOr modifying `Change` to `OK` seems like a simple option so that the button becomes generic for both cases without introducing the parameter.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comme